	<h2>Why Spreadsheet Audits are a Lifestyle Leak</h2>
	<p>
		Many store owners attempt to solve this by setting up complex spreadsheets or scheduling weekly staff audits. However, manual processes have several critical flaws:
	</p>
	<ul>
		<li><strong>High Cognitive Load:</strong> Shifting your focus from creative or strategic tasks to search raw spreadsheets takes a heavy mental toll. It creates fatigue and increases operational stress.</li>
		<li><strong>Lagging Information:</strong> By the time you notice an error at the end of the week, your memory of the events is stale, making reconciliation take twice as long.</li>
		<li><strong>Incomplete Data:</strong> Paper and spreadsheets don't log automatically. A missed entry means the entire audit process fails, forcing you to recount from scratch.</li>
	</ul>
	
